  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1234 PM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nOur area will have a continuation of hot and dry conditions, as a \nlarge upper high remains our dominant weather influence with its\nassociated subsidence. The high will remain centered over the \nlower Mississippi Valley through the end of this week and into the\nweekend. In the early part of next week, the center of this high \nis forecast to shift northwest over the Red River Valley.\nTemperature forecast is generally persistence with overnight lows\nin the 70s and highs ranging from the mid 90s in our southern \ncounties, to 100-103 in most of the Big Country and portions of \nthe Concho Valley. Somewhat breezy conditions are expected \nThursday and Friday with south winds. Surface pressure gradient \nwill be a little weaker over the weekend into early next week, so \nexpect south winds to be comparatively lower during that time \nframe.",
